  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening UNESCO sites in Central America and Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNESCO sites are territories of vital ecological, geological and cultural importance, and are key to sustainable development. The local and indigenous communities living in these territories rely extensively on their ecosystem services such as water, tourism, natural resources and increase resilience of people to global challenges. Promotion of more equitable, sustainable and greener societies to building peace, creating knowledge and understanding through science to face climate change, pollution and environmental challenges in UNESCO sites, through international cooperation.
Strengthening of Biosphere Reserves, Geoparks and World Heritage networks in Central America, Mexico and Colombia (sustainable development and Agenda 2030, building resilience, governance, inclusion, cooperation and contributing to biodiversity and climate action agendas).</narrative>
  </description>
